# NeuroFlow — Core Standards

NeuroFlow is a **facilitation portal** for neuroscience medical image processing. Optimize UX/UI for **reading, writing, and manipulating neuroimaging data**, especially **MRI**.

- Prefer clarity over feature density; surface BIDS metadata (subject, session, modality, pipeline status) alongside volumes.
- Treat data as sensitive: no PHI in logs; least-privilege access; document handling assumptions.
- **English only** for code, comments, docstrings, commits, and API schemas. UI copy defaults to English.

## Repo hygiene

- Small, focused changes; match existing layout.
- No secrets in git; use `.env` + `.env.example`.
- Document licenses for third-party neuroimaging tools.
- Update tests and user-visible docs (`assets/DESIGN.md`, `doc/mockup/`) when behavior changes.

## Specialized rules (apply by file type)

| Rule | When |
|------|------|
| `bids.mdc` | BIDS datasets, derivatives, layout code |
| `backend.mdc` | Python, API, Poetry |
| `frontend.mdc` | HTML/CSS, mockups, design system |
| `docker.mdc` | Processing images and orchestration |

## Stack (summary)

BIDS data · Poetry + FastAPI · HTML/Tailwind · Docker pipelines · pytest · Rich · NiBabel/pybids
